Q: Take integer inputs till the user enters 0 and print the sum of all numbers (HINT: while loop) A: <pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>package com.dev.java;

import java.util.Scanner;

public class SumofNintegers {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // TODO Auto-generated method stub

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print(&quot;Please enter the Numbers you want to add: &quot;);
        int a = sc.nextInt();
        int sum = 0;

        while(a&gt;=0) {
            if(a==0) {
                break;
            }
            else {
                sum = a + sum;
            }
            a = sc.nextInt();
        }
        System.out.println(&quot;The sum of given numbers is: &quot;+sum);
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Disabling load-styles.php file in Wordpress A: <p>If you are confused about, for example, the CSS added on HTML forms by WordPress automatically:</p>
<pre><code>input[type=color], input[type=date], input[type=datetime-local], input[type=datetime], input[type=email], input[type=month], input[type=number], input[type=password], input[type=search], input[type=tel], input[type=text], input[type=time], input[type=url], input[type=week], select, textarea {
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 transparent;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid #8c8f94;
    background-color: #fff;
    color: #2c3338;
}
</code></pre>
<p>For example, it makes my form strange:</p>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/OTfQiR18.png" alt="strange result" /></p>
<p>CSS above is from <code>http://localhost:8080/wp-admin/load-styles.php?c=0&amp;dir=ltr&amp;load%5Bchunk_0%5D=dashicons,admin-bar,common,forms,admin-menu,dashboard,...&amp;ver=6.9</code> .</p>
<p>Then I noticed if I manually  remove <code>forms</code> from it, using <code>http://localhost:8080/wp-admin/load-styles.php?c=0&amp;dir=ltr&amp;load%5Bchunk_0%5D=dashicons,admin-bar,common,admin-menu,dashboard,...&amp;ver=6.9</code> , I will get a clean form without default CSS by WordPress, and still get a normal WordPress admin page.</p>
<p>So I read some of the WordPress core code. My code below will only remove <code>forms</code> from this url.</p>
<pre><code>add_filter( 'print_admin_styles', function () {
    $wp_styles         = wp_styles();
    $wp_styles-&gt;concat = str_replace( 'forms,', '', $wp_styles-&gt;concat );

    return true;
} );
</code></pre>
<p>Now it looks better:</p>
<p><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/pBnudswf.png" alt="fixed result" /></p>
<p>Put it in your <code>functions.php</code> or your plugin php file. That is all you need. This will remove <code>forms</code> from all admin pages.</p>

